<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<chapter xmlns="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook" id="chapter-xpath-and-controls" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
    <title>XPath and Controls</title>
    <para>This chapter maps XForms XPath semantics to XPath 3.1 execution in SaxonForms and explains control rendering and interaction patterns for standard and custom controls.</para>

    <section id="chapter-xpath-mapping">
        <title>XPath expression mapping</title>
        <para>SaxonForms translates XForms XPath expressions into XPath 3.1 at evaluation time through a function-rewriting pipeline. The central rewriting function is <literal>xforms:impose()</literal> in <literal>src/xforms-function-library.xsl</literal>, which rewrites XForms function calls to their <literal>xforms:</literal>-prefixed XSLT equivalents so SaxonJS can evaluate them natively.</para>

        <section id="chapter-xpath-function-rewriting">
            <title>Function rewriting (<literal>xforms:impose</literal>)</title>
            <para>When a binding expression or calculate attribute is evaluated, <literal>xforms:impose()</literal> performs string-level substitution of XForms function names to their <literal>xforms:</literal> namespace counterparts. For example, <literal>instance('foo')</literal> is rewritten to <literal>xforms:instance('foo')</literal>, which resolves to the XSLT function <literal>xforms:instance()</literal> in <literal>src/xforms-function-library.xsl</literal>.</para>
            <para>The <literal>xforms:resolve-index()</literal> function in <literal>src/xforms-function-library.xsl</literal> handles repeat index substitution: expressions containing <literal>index('repeatId')</literal> are replaced with the current integer index value before evaluation. This avoids runtime resolution issues where <literal>index()</literal> would need repeat context that is unavailable in a static XPath 3.1 call.</para>
        </section>

        <section id="chapter-xpath-context-resolution">
            <title>Context resolution in repeat and action scopes</title>
            <para>XPath evaluation is dispatched through <literal>xforms:evaluate-xpath-with-context-node()</literal> in <literal>src/saxon-xforms.xsl</literal>, which accepts the expression string, a context node from the bound instance, and the namespace context for prefix resolution. The related <literal>xforms:evaluate-xpath-with-instance-id()</literal> function resolves the instance element first.</para>
            <para>Within repeats, context resolution relies on positional information. The
                    <literal>xforms:resolveXPathStrings()</literal> function in
                    <literal>src/saxon-xforms.xsl</literal> resolves relative paths against the
                current repeat context node. The
                    <literal>position()</literal>/<literal>last()</literal> substitution
                pre-computes positional values in bind calculate expressions before
                evaluation.</para>
        </section>

        <section id="chapter-xpath-function-library">
            <title>XForms function library</title>
            <para>XForms 1.1 adds functions beyond the XPath 1.0 core library (see
                    <ulink url="https://www.w3.org/TR/xforms11/#expr-lib">XForms 1.1 §7.6+</ulink>).
                SaxonForms either rewrites those bare names to <literal>xforms:</literal> XSLT
                functions, rewrites them by expression transform, or leaves them to native SaxonJS
                XPath 3.1 evaluation. This section inventories every XForms 1.1-defined additional
                function. It does not catalog the full XPath 1.0 core set or extra XPath 3.1-only
                features.</para>

            <para>Implementation packages:</para>
            <itemizedlist>
                <listitem><para><literal>src/xforms-function-library.xsl</literal> — rewrite gate
                            (<literal>xforms:impose</literal>, <literal>$xform-functions</literal>),
                        runtime/context functions, and NaN-safe numeric wrappers.</para></listitem>
                <listitem><para><literal>src/xforms-xpath-functions.xsl</literal> — pure XPath 3.1
                        implementations of most remaining XForms 1.1 functions, plus JS-bridged
                            <literal>digest</literal>/<literal>hmac</literal>.</para></listitem>
            </itemizedlist>

            <section id="chapter-xpath-function-disposition">
                <title>Disposition model</title>
                <para>Each XForms 1.1 additional function has one disposition:</para>
                <variablelist>
                    <varlistentry>
                        <term>Implemented</term>
                        <listitem><para>Bare name is listed in <literal>$xform-functions</literal>, so
                                    <literal>xforms:impose()</literal> rewrites
                                    <literal>name(…)</literal> to <literal>xforms:name(…)</literal>,
                                and an <literal>xsl:function name="xforms:name"</literal> exists.
                                Wrappers that delegate to XPath 3.1 still count as Implemented when
                                the rewrite and wrapper adjust XForms semantics (for example NaN on
                                empty <literal>min</literal>/<literal>max</literal>).</para></listitem>
                    </varlistentry>
                    <varlistentry>
                        <term>Rewritten (non-function)</term>
                        <listitem><para>No <literal>xsl:function</literal>;
                                    <literal>xforms:impose()</literal> rewrites the call site to an
                                XPath 3.1 expression (used for <literal>current()</literal>).</para></listitem>
                    </varlistentry>
                    <varlistentry>
                        <term>Fall-through</term>
                        <listitem><para>Name is not registered for rewrite. Evaluation uses the native
                                SaxonJS default function namespace (XPath 3.1 F&amp;O). Divergences
                                versus the XForms 1.1 definition are listed only for these
                                entries.</para></listitem>
                    </varlistentry>
                </variablelist>
                <para>XPath 1.0 core names that XForms inherits (<literal>count</literal>,
                        <literal>sum</literal>, <literal>string</literal>, <literal>boolean</literal>,
                        <literal>number</literal>, <literal>true</literal>/<literal>false</literal>,
                    string functions, and so on) are not rewritten. They execute as native XPath 3.1
                    equivalents. Common empty-sequence and type-error differences versus XPath 1.0
                    / XForms-era expectations are summarized under fall-through notes; SaxonForms
                    also wraps some MIP calculate evaluation in try/catch so empty-string arithmetic
                    yields NaN rather than a hard type error (see Conformance).</para>
            </section>

