            <section id="chapter-xpath-function-fallthrough">
                <title>Fall-through divergence notes</title>
                <para>Only fall-through names are compared here. Extra XPath 3.1 capabilities are
                    assumed and not listed.</para>

                <section id="chapter-xpath-fallthrough-compare">
                    <title><literal>compare()</literal> (XForms 1.1 §7.7.8 → XPath 3.1
                            <literal>fn:compare</literal>)</title>
                    <para>XForms 1.1 defines
                            <literal>number compare(string, string)</literal>: return
                            <literal>-1</literal>, <literal>0</literal>, or <literal>1</literal> from
                        lexicographic comparison using Unicode code point values.</para>
                    <para>XPath 3.1 <ulink url="https://www.w3.org/TR/xpath-functions-31/#func-compare"
                                ><literal>fn:compare</literal></ulink> is
                            <literal>xs:integer? compare(xs:string?, xs:string?)</literal> with an
                        optional third collation argument. Divergences that matter for authors:</para>
                    <itemizedlist>
                        <listitem><para><emphasis>Empty arguments</emphasis> — XPath returns the empty
                                sequence if either argument is the empty sequence. XForms 1.1 is
                                specified in the XPath 1.0 type system (string arguments always have a
                                string value); empty-node string-value is <literal>""</literal>, not
                                empty sequence. Forms that pass true empty sequences can therefore
                                see empty results under fall-through where a pure XForms processor
                                would still return a number.</para></listitem>
                        <listitem><para><emphasis>Collation</emphasis> — XForms requires Unicode code
                                point order. XPath uses the default (or explicit) collation. For the
                                BMP code-point-equal cases exercised by W3C 7.7.8.a this matches in
                                practice; collation-sensitive locales can diverge.</para></listitem>
                        <listitem><para><emphasis>Arity</emphasis> — XPath accepts an optional collation
                                URI third argument. XForms has only the two-string form. Extra-arg
                                calls are an XPath extension relative to XForms 1.1, not a SaxonForms
                                rewrite.</para></listitem>
                    </itemizedlist>
                    <para>There is no SaxonForms wrapper today; improving strict XForms code-point
                        semantics would mean adding <literal>compare</literal> to
                            <literal>$xform-functions</literal> and an
                            <literal>xforms:compare</literal> implementation.</para>
                </section>

                <section id="chapter-xpath-fallthrough-xpath10-core">
                    <title>Inherited XPath 1.0 core names (summary)</title>
                    <para>Unrewritten core names evaluate as XPath 3.1. Divergences authors most often
                        hit versus XPath 1.0 / XForms-era expectations:</para>
                    <itemizedlist>
                        <listitem><para><emphasis>Empty sequences and arithmetic</emphasis> — XPath 3.1
                                type errors replace many XPath 1.0 NaN results. MIP calculate paths in
                                SaxonForms mitigate this with try/catch → NaN (implementation-defined;
                                see Conformance).</para></listitem>
                        <listitem><para><emphasis><literal>sum</literal> on empty</emphasis> — XPath 3.1
                                    <literal>fn:sum(())</literal> returns <literal>0</literal> by
                                default (optional second argument); XPath 1.0 returned
                                <literal>0</literal> as well for empty node-sets, so this is usually
                                compatible.</para></listitem>
                        <listitem><para><emphasis>Node-set vs sequence</emphasis> — duplicate nodes and
                                atomization follow XPath 3.1 rules when expressions are richer than
                                XPath 1.0 PathExpr.</para></listitem>
                    </itemizedlist>
                    <para>These core names are fall-through by design; they are not individually
                        wrapped unless an XForms additional function of the same local name exists
                        (as with <literal>avg</literal>/<literal>min</literal>/<literal>max</literal>
                        / <literal>id</literal>).</para>
                </section>
            </section>

            <section id="chapter-xpath-function-impl-notes">
                <title>Implementation notes (Implemented / Rewritten, not fall-through)</title>
                <para>These callouts document intentional wrapper behavior. They are not fall-through
                    divergences, because calls are rewritten to <literal>xforms:*</literal>.</para>
                <itemizedlist>
                    <listitem><para><literal>min</literal>/<literal>max</literal>/<literal>avg</literal>
                            — empty or non-numeric input yields <literal>NaN</literal> (XForms 1.1),
                            not XPath 3.1 empty sequence / type error from bare
                                <literal>fn:min</literal>/<literal>fn:max</literal>/<literal>fn:avg</literal>.</para></listitem>
                    <listitem><para><literal>id</literal> — unions standard <literal>fn:id</literal>
                            results with <literal>@xml:id</literal> and elements typed
                                <literal>xsd:ID</literal> via <literal>xsi:type</literal>.</para></listitem>
                    <listitem><para><literal>if</literal> — XForms function form
                                <literal>if(test, a, b)</literal> with string-oriented XForms 1.1
                            signature; distinct from XPath <literal>if (test) then a else b</literal>.
                            As an XSLT function, both branch arguments are evaluated before the call
                            (no short-circuit at the function boundary).</para></listitem>
                    <listitem><para><literal>choose</literal> — XForms requires both result arguments to
                            be evaluated; matches function-call evaluation. Prefer XPath
                                <literal>if then else</literal> when short-circuit matters.</para></listitem>
                    <listitem><para><literal>power</literal> — delegates to
                            <literal>math:pow</literal>.</para></listitem>
                    <listitem><para><literal>adjust-dateTime-to-timezone</literal> — string in/out; 0-arity
                            overload returns <literal>""</literal>. Distinct from typed F&amp;O
                                <literal>fn:adjust-dateTime-to-timezone</literal> signatures even though
                            the one-arg path calls that function internally after casting.</para></listitem>
                    <listitem><para><literal>seconds-from-dateTime</literal> — XForms epoch-seconds
                            semantics. Same local name as XPath 3.1
                                <literal>fn:seconds-from-dateTime</literal> (seconds component of a
                                <literal>xs:dateTime</literal>). Rewrite registration ensures bare
                            XForms calls use the XForms meaning.</para></listitem>
                    <listitem><para><literal>current()</literal> — rewrite captures outermost context item;
                            not XSLT <literal>fn:current()</literal>.</para></listitem>
                    <listitem><para><literal>digest</literal>/<literal>hmac</literal> — require the JS crypto
                            bridge (<literal>@noble/hashes</literal> / available subtle crypto). Empty
                            string when the library is unavailable; secure context needed in
                            browsers.</para></listitem>
                    <listitem><para><literal>random</literal> — optional seed parameter accepted and ignored;
                            always <literal>Math.random()</literal>.</para></listitem>
                    <listitem><para><literal>context</literal> — current implementation returns
                                <literal>.</literal> (context item). Full XForms action/UI context-node
                            semantics still depend on how the evaluator sets the XPath context when the
                            expression runs.</para></listitem>
                </itemizedlist>
            </section>
        </section>
    </section>

    <section id="chapter-controls-mapping">
        <title>Controls and rendering model</title>
        <para>SaxonForms maps each XForms control element to an HTML element via <literal>get-html</literal> mode templates. The control rendering entry point is the control-match template in <literal>src/saxon-xforms.xsl</literal>, which processes all XForms control elements and delegates to <literal>get-html</literal> mode for HTML output generation.</para>
        <para>The diagram below maps each XForms control to its HTML output element and the DOM event handlers that wire interactive behavior back into the action dispatch pipeline.</para>
        <mediaobject>
            <imageobject>
                <imagedata fileref="../diagrams/controls-html-mapping.svg" format="SVG" width="100%" scalefit="1"/>
            </imageobject>
        </mediaobject>

        <section id="chapter-controls-core">
            <title>Core form controls</title>
            <para>Each core control template resolves its data binding via the <literal>get-properties</literal> mode template in <literal>src/saxon-xforms.xsl</literal>, which returns a map containing the bound nodeset, instance context, and matching bind element. Key control templates:</para>
            <itemizedlist>
                <listitem><para><literal>xforms:input</literal> template in <literal>src/saxon-xforms.xsl</literal> — Renders <literal>&lt;input&gt;</literal> with type derived from XSD type (<literal>xs:date</literal> → <literal>type="date"</literal>, <literal>xs:boolean</literal> → <literal>type="checkbox"</literal>). Supports incremental mode via <literal>ixsl:onkeyup</literal> handlers.</para></listitem>
                <listitem><para><literal>xforms:output</literal> template in <literal>src/saxon-xforms.xsl</literal> — Renders <literal>&lt;span&gt;</literal> with computed value. Supports <literal>@mediatype</literal> for image rendering and <literal>@value</literal> attribute for XPath expression evaluation.</para></listitem>
                <listitem><para><literal>xforms:select</literal>/<literal>xforms:select1</literal> templates in <literal>src/saxon-xforms.xsl</literal> — Render <literal>&lt;select&gt;</literal> (multi/single). Handle <literal>xforms:item</literal>, <literal>xforms:choices</literal>, and <literal>xforms:itemset</literal> child elements. Non-incremental select uses blur/focusout handlers for deferred update.</para></listitem>
                <listitem><para><literal>xforms:textarea</literal> template in <literal>src/saxon-xforms.xsl</literal> — Renders <literal>&lt;textarea&gt;</literal>.</para></listitem>
                <listitem><para><literal>xforms:range</literal> template in <literal>src/saxon-xforms.xsl</literal> — Renders <literal>&lt;input type="range"&gt;</literal>. Incremental mode uses <literal>ixsl:oninput</literal> handlers.</para></listitem>
                <listitem><para><literal>xforms:upload</literal> template in <literal>src/saxon-xforms.xsl</literal> — Renders <literal>&lt;input type="file"&gt;</literal>. File content is parsed via <literal>readFileAsXML()</literal> in <literal>xforms-javascript-library.xsl</literal> and inserted into the bound instance node.</para></listitem>
                <listitem><para><literal>xforms:trigger</literal> template in <literal>src/saxon-xforms.xsl</literal> — Renders <literal>&lt;button&gt;</literal> or <literal>&lt;a&gt;</literal> with <literal>data-action</literal> attribute. Onclick dispatches <literal>DOMActivate</literal>.</para></listitem>
                <listitem><para><literal>xforms:submit</literal> template in <literal>src/saxon-xforms.xsl</literal> — Renders <literal>&lt;button data-submit&gt;</literal>. Onclick triggers submission flow.</para></listitem>
            </itemizedlist>
        </section>

        <section id="chapter-controls-container">
            <title>Container controls</title>
            <itemizedlist>
                <listitem><para><literal>xforms:group</literal> template in <literal>src/saxon-xforms.xsl</literal> — Renders <literal>&lt;div class="xforms-group"&gt;</literal>. Supports <literal>@ref</literal> for scoped context and <literal>relevant</literal> hiding.</para></listitem>
                <listitem><para><literal>xforms:repeat</literal> template in <literal>src/saxon-xforms.xsl</literal> — Renders iterable <literal>&lt;div data-repeatable-context&gt;</literal> with <literal>data-repeat-item</literal> children. Repeat index is tracked and updated on click events. Refresh is handled by <literal>refreshRepeats-JS</literal>.</para></listitem>
                <listitem><para><literal>xforms:switch</literal>/<literal>xforms:case</literal> templates in <literal>src/saxon-xforms.xsl</literal> — Render <literal>&lt;div class="xforms-switch"&gt;</literal> with cases shown/hidden. The <literal>action-toggle</literal> template controls case visibility. Known issue: toggle inside repeat affects all iterations (9.3.1.f).</para></listitem>
            </itemizedlist>
        </section>

        <section id="chapter-controls-custom">
            <title>Custom controls and fork enhancements</title>
            <para>The fork adds several controls and behaviors not present in upstream Saxon-Forms:</para>
            <itemizedlist>
                <listitem><para><literal>xf:script</literal> action (<literal>action-script</literal> template in <literal>src/saxon-xforms.xsl</literal>) — XForms 2.0 script execution via <literal>ixsl:call(window, 'eval', ...)</literal>.</para></listitem>
                <listitem><para><literal>xf:load</literal> action (<literal>action-load</literal> template in <literal>src/saxon-xforms.xsl</literal>) — Supports <literal>show="new"</literal>, <literal>show="replace"</literal>, and <literal>javascript:</literal> URI scheme.</para></listitem>
                <listitem><para>Namespace prefix propagation — XPaths can use prefixes declared on <literal>&lt;xf:xform&gt;</literal> (e.g., <literal>o:catalog</literal> instead of <literal>*:catalog</literal>). Implemented via <literal>addNamespaceDeclarationsToDocument()</literal> in <literal>src/saxon-xforms.xsl</literal>.</para></listitem>
            </itemizedlist>
        </section>
    </section>
</chapter>
